{
  "verdict": "divergent",
  "divergences": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "The source's “Conversely” starts with a feedforward system. Lean does not even require that the nonconscious system's behaviour have a feedforward realization. In fact, Target requires every S1 behaviour to have a D11 realization: take Q to mean “my behaviour has a D11 realization.” If any behaviour lacked one, Q would meet both hypotheses yet be inferable exactly from the behaviour. This matters because N.d4 describes one system processing inputs online at all finite lengths. Such a system can retain an input bit indefinitely, which no finite acyclic S1 can do. Appendix A's construction starting from a feedforward implementation of x → F(x) does not state this result for arbitrary online behaviours."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "As declared, D11 is a proxy for the consciousness-sufficient structure, not an IIT criterion. It requires the entire nonempty update-dependency graph to be strongly connected, with positive-length return paths, and counts dependencies even at unreachable states. The source's insertion of a ϕ-increasing device does not specify that graph condition."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean idealizes an inference as an arbitrary binary predicate on the complete behaviour function, whether or not an experiment could evaluate it. This is a natural strengthening of the source's indistinguishability point: identical functions agree under even these predicates."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean explicitly assumes an inhabited input type, as declared; the passage does not state that qualification."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The disagreement conclusion has the advertised direction. The substantive difference is its scope: a converse construction on feedforward systems becomes a requirement that integrated systems cover every behaviour of an unrestricted-duration S1 system."
}
